  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions about electricians in Anna</h2>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Who is the best electrician for Anna, TX?</h3><p>Our top pick for 2026 is ABR Electric, based in McKinney. It's the only company in our comparison with a Texas Electrical Contractor License number (TECL #27762) published directly on its own site, and it's a certified Tesla installer — useful if you're adding an EV charger in a newer Anna subdivision. Top Notch Electrician (Licensed Master Electrician, 13 Yelp reviews) is a solid second option.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Do I need a permit for electrical work in Anna, TX?</h3><p>Yes. Panel upgrades, service changes and most new circuits require a permit and inspection through the City of Anna, and Oncor typically needs to disconnect and reconnect service for panel swaps. A licensed electrician should pull the permit as part of the job.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Why does Anna need more electricians with EV-charger experience?</h3><p>Anna's newer subdivisions east of US-75, including Camden Parc and Avery Pointe, are adding homes with attached garages built for Level 2 EV chargers, which typically require a dedicated 240-volt circuit and, in older homes, a panel upgrade to support the added load.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>How much does a panel upgrade cost in Anna?</h3><p>A 100-amp to 200-amp panel upgrade typically runs $2,500–$4,500 installed across DFW, including the panel, meter base, grounding, labor and permit. Simple like-for-like swaps start closer to $1,800.</p></div>
